<div class="wrap page-head">
  <p class="eyebrow">Early Years · 20 months to 4 years</p>
  <h1>Play is the work</h1>
  <p class="lede">Our Nursery and Kindergarten groups spend the day in English, mostly outside, mostly playing. We follow the British Early Years Foundation Stage framework, which is a careful way of saying we watch what each child is ready for and set it up.</p>
</div>

<section class="band--paper">
  <div class="wrap two two--flip">
    <div class="photo photo--blob" data-caption="photo: Nursery outside, water play or the sand pit"></div>
    <div>
      <h2>What a morning looks like</h2>
      <p>Children arrive, choose something to do, and are quietly steered toward what they need: a story, a song, a tricky puzzle, a friend they have not played with yet. There is a snack, a run outside, and a short group time with phonics or counting hidden inside a game.</p>
      <p>The youngest ones can do a partial day and go home after lunch. Everyone naps or rests in the early afternoon.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

